Politifact:politifact14071,"Lindsey Graham Threatens To Convert To Democrat If Republicans Don’t Dump Trump – True Trumpers 28 captures 22 Mar 2017 - 29 Jan 2023 Feb MAR Apr 22 2016 2017 2018 success fail About this capture TIMESTAMPS The Wayback Machine - https://web.archive.org/web/20170322070001/http://truetrumpers.com/lindsey-graham-threatens-to-convert-to-democrat-if-republicans-dont-dump-trump 1 Home MyViews Views True Trumpers Home News Economics Polls Sports Breaking News Excellent News For Veterans In March, 2017 BREAKING – Trump is BOYCOTTING the UN. Do You Support? Crazy Glenn Beck Goes Full PC – Defends Muslims from Trump’s Temporary Travel Ban Michelle Obama Says I Will Be 46th President Of The U.S In 2020. Would You Support Her? BREAKING: Two Muslim Rapes White Girl . (VIDEO) Would You Support Trump If He Deport All Of Them? BREAKING: Trump Just Fired James Comey. Do You Support This ? BREAKING: Trump Just Fired James Comey. Do You Support This ? EXPOSED – ‘Black Lives’ Leader Arrested On SHOCKING Charges, National Media Hides It BREAKING: Muslim migrants in U.S rape Russian Child For 30 Hours, Then Kills Her . Do You Support Deport Of Them ? KING: Donald Trump Should Be Immediately Removed From Office Home / Uncategorized / Lindsey Graham Threatens To Convert To Democrat If Republicans Don’t Dump Trump Lindsey Graham Threatens To Convert To Democrat If Republicans Don’t Dump Trump 19 hours ago Uncategorized During a time when the Republican Party’s presumptive nominee, Donald Trump, should be working to bring the party together and prepare for the primary battle against Hillary Clinton, he continues to deepen the divide between Republicans and Americans alike. Trump’s recent attack on U.S. District Judge Gonzalo Curiel because of his Mexican-American background prompted Sen. Lindsey Graham to round up the Republicans who have previously endorsed Donald Trump, and persuade them to take it all back. Graham claimed that Trump’s racist remarks were “the most un-American thing from a politician since Joe McCarthy.” “If anybody was looking for an off-ramp, this is probably it,” Graham told The New York Times.” Senator Graham elaborated on this during an interview with NBC News’ Hallie Jackson. “There are a lot of people who want to be loyal to the Republican Party, including me,” he said. “But there’ll come a point in time where we’re gonna have to understand that it’s not just about the 2016 race, it’s about the future of the party and I would like to support our nominee. I just can’t.” Donald Trump claimed that Judge Gonzalo Curiel, who is presiding over the Trump University case, has been biased toward him because of his Latino heritage. “I couldn’t disagree more with a statement like that,” Senate Majority Leader Mitch McConnell (R-Ky.) said Sunday. “Those kinds of comments are very serious to me,” Rep. Susan Collins (R-Maine) said to News radio WGAN. “They are completely unacceptable, and what they indicate — which is why I think this is so serious — is a lack of respect for our judicial system and for the separation of powers doctrine that is enshrined in the Constitution.” Although many Republicans, including House Speaker Paul Ryan, have condemned Trump’s accusations, they continue to support him. Share this: Click to share on Twitter (Opens in new window) Click to share on Facebook (Opens in new window) Click to share on Google+ (Opens in new window) Related 2017-03-21 systemofadown Share Facebook Twitter Google + Stumbleupon LinkedIn Pinterest Previous Poll:Do you think that Obama deserves the ‘Presidental Pension’?? Next Muslim migrants in Germany rape Russian child for 30 hours, then get “massacred” by angry Russians in reprisal Related Articles Excellent News For Veterans In March, 2017 8 mins ago BREAKING – Trump is BOYCOTTING the UN. Do You Support? 15 mins ago Crazy Glenn Beck Goes Full PC – Defends Muslims from Trump’s Temporary Travel Ban 20 mins ago Check Also Michelle Obama Says I Will Be 46th Pres