Politifact:politifact14991,"Fact-Check: No, Fall River, Massachusetts, Was Not 'Built by Immigrants' Enable Accessibility Skip to Content Newsletters B America 250 American Tributes American Soundtrack 250 Years of History Business of America 250 News Culture Entertainment Media Tech Sports B Inspired Politics Politics On the Hill On the Hill Articles On The Hill Exclusive Video Wires Economy World London / Europe Border / Cartel Chronicles Israel / Middle East Africa Asia Latin America All World Video BREITBART Newsletters B America 250 American Tributes American Soundtrack 250 Years of History Business of America 250 News Culture Entertainment Media Tech Sports B Inspired Politics Politics On the Hill On the Hill Articles On The Hill Exclusive Video Wires Economy World London / Europe Border / Cartel Chronicles Israel / Middle East Africa Asia Latin America World News Video Radio / Podcasts The Alex Marlow Show Breitbart News Daily About Us BREITBART Politics is downstream from culture Andrew Breitbart Midterm Elections Russia Plague Outbreak Cornell Rape Case Iran War France Riots Fact-Check: No, Fall River, Massachusetts, Was Not ‘Built by Immigrants’ 46,018 Ian Mason 30 Jan 2018 Joe Kennedy Talks Spanish to DACA Illegal Aliens: ‘We Will Fight For You!’ ‘Build A Wall And My Generation Will Tear It Down:’ Joe Kennedy Recalls Woke Anti-Trump... Fact-Check: No, Fall River, Massachusetts, Was Not ‘Built by Immigrants’ ICONIC: North Korean Dissident Ji Seong-Ho Holds Up Crutches After President Trump Praises Him in... Trump in SOTU Address: ‘It Is Time’ for Merit-Based Legal Immigration Rep. Joe Kennedy III (D-MA) claimed the host-city of his response to President Donald Trump’s State of the Union address, Fall River, Massachusetts was “built by immigrants.” Fact-Check: MOSTLY FALSE What is now Fall River was first established in the 1600s by English settlers who were not “immigrants” but colonists. A native-born family, the Bordens ran a mill in what became the town for generations before and after the American revolution. Industrialization began when Col. Joseph Durfee, a native-born Revolutionary War hero built the first factory in 1811. Later, at the end of the 19th Century a wave of immigrants swelled the town’s population. Immigrants, however, never made up a majority of the population of Bristol County, where Fall River lies, even at their early 20th Century peak. Immigration Politics immigration Joe Kennedy III SOTU COMMENTS Please let us know if you're having issues with commenting. SOCIAL MOST POPULAR Bessent: Iran Faces Zero Oil Revenue This Week — Tehran Warns of Crisis Rasmussen Poll Gives Republicans Edge Among Hispanic Voters Fort Hood Attacker Nidal Hasan to Be Executed by Firing Squad Claire Valdez Says She Pitched 'Trans Bill of Rights' to Hakeem Jeffries Americans Turn to AI Chatbots to Decide How to Vote in Midterm Elections Trump: ‘Threat’ Forced U.S. Bombers from UK; Iran Will ‘Suffer Greatly Teen Farage Supporter Arrested over Online Jokes About Tory Politician VIDEO: New York Declares Statewide Emergency to 'Confront' Measles Outbreak Border Security, Public Safety, and American Sovereignty Markwayne Mulllin Russian Lab Worker Dead, 200 Under Observation After Suspected Leak FROM THE HOMEPAGE Exclusive — Sec. Markwayne Mullin: DHS Employing ‘Equipment That I Can’t Talk About’ at Border Exclusive — CBP Commissioner Rodney Scott on Border Enforcement: ‘Pretty Simple, Its Night and Day’ Between Trump and Biden Admins Germany Arrests Spy Boss and His Former Chief of Staff For Treason, Espionage Teen Farage Supporter Arrested over Social Media Jokes About Tory Politician Cornell brings in ex-Justice official Sally Yates to review school’s handling of sex assault claims Nolte: Leftist Cornell Faculty Prepares ‘No Confidence’ Vote Against Leftist Cornell University Rasmussen Poll Gives Republicans Edge Among Hispanic Voters Report: Hackers Use Chinese AI Agents to Breach South Korean Banks No Thanks: Russia Offers to Help Fight Measles in U.S. After Plague Lab Incident Paychecks Rose For Third Straight Month in August—Even After Inflation Hostin: Trump Is ‘Deranged,’ Might Be Time for the 25th Amendment The Athletic Calls for the Fever to ‘Part’ with Sophie Cunningham Because Her Takes Are ‘Too Turbulent’ BREITBART NEWS Masthead About Us Accessibility Statement Policy Info Editorial Guidelines Terms of Use Privacy Policy Advertise Contact Us Careers Store Get the App Newsletters Signup Send A Tip Sitemap Copyright © 2026 Breitbart",1,Politifact,train
