Politifact:politifact14664,"ICE Detainer Issued for Suspected Wine Country Arsonist in Sonoma Jail Enable Accessibility Skip to Content Newsletters B America 250 American Tributes American Soundtrack 250 Years of History Business of America 250 News Culture Entertainment Media Tech Sports B Inspired Politics Politics On the Hill On the Hill Articles On The Hill Exclusive Video Wires Economy World London / Europe Border / Cartel Chronicles Israel / Middle East Africa Asia Latin America All World Video BREITBART Newsletters B America 250 American Tributes American Soundtrack 250 Years of History Business of America 250 News Culture Entertainment Media Tech Sports B Inspired Politics Politics On the Hill On the Hill Articles On The Hill Exclusive Video Wires Economy World London / Europe Border / Cartel Chronicles Israel / Middle East Africa Asia Latin America World News Video Radio / Podcasts The Alex Marlow Show Breitbart News Daily About Us BREITBART Politics is downstream from culture Andrew Breitbart Brazil Election Results Midterm Elections Iran War Cornell Rape Case super intelligence ICE Detainer Issued for Suspected Wine Country Arsonist in Sonoma Jail 59,252 David McNew / Getty Chriss W. Street 17 Oct 2017 UPDATE: Consistent with our subsequent coverage of the California wildfires, this story has been updated to clarify that Jesus Fabian Gonzales is not suspected of the recent Sonoma County fires that killed 40 residents. The U.S. Immigration & Customs Enforcement Agency (ICE) issued a detainer request on the Sonoma County Jail for Jesus Fabian Gonzalez, who was arrested Sunday on suspicion of arson in Wine Country fires. Breitbart News reported earlier this week that Sonoma County Sheriffs had arrested Jesus Fabian Gonzalez, 29, at Maxwell Regional Park in Sonoma County after a series of reports of ongoing fires in the region. Mr. Gonzalez was observed around 3:00 p.m. PDT wearing a jacket and walking “out of the creek area and a plume of smoke behind him,” according to the Santa Rosa Press Democrat . Mr. Gonzalez, who is homeless and reportedly known by law enforcement to have been living under a nearby bridge, claimed he was cold and had lit the fire to stay warm. But it was a balmy 78 degrees when he and the plume of smoke were first observed. Mr. Gonzalez was booked into the Sonoma County Jail for suspicion of felony arson. His bail was set at a steep $110,000, according to the Sonoma County Sheriff Public Information Officer. Sargent Spencer Crum told Breitbart that Mr. Gonzalez is also on a U.S. Immigration & Customs Enforcement Agency (ICE) detainer request, despite Sonoma County declaring itself as a “sanctuary county” in May 2014. The county only cooperates with “ICE holds” if the prisoner has been convicted of a felony or any misdemeanor offence that falls within the Trust Act within the last five years. Mr. Gonzalez’s immigration status has not yet been announced. The American Civil Liberties Union argues detainers are a violation of “ unreasonable searches and seizures ” under the U.S. Constitution’s Fourth Amendment . The Sonoma County Sheriff Department’s “1.0 Policy Statement” reads: “No person shall be held solely on the basis of their immigration status.” The policy adds that “the immigration status of a person, and the lack of immigration documentation, should have no bearing on the manner in which Sheriff’s Office personnel execute their duties.” According to ICE documents , Sonoma County declined 491 detainer requests in 2014 and 2015. During the 2017 period from January 28 through February 3, when President Donald Trump issued his immigration Executive Order 13768 to require all federal, state and local government to comply with ICE detainers, Sonoma County still denied detainers. Sonoma County fires have killed dozens. 172 are still missing and 102,000 residents have been dislocated — about one-fifth of the entire population. The latest financial losses include 3,819 unincorporated parcels with 100 structures valued at $2,016,962,239, and 2,907 homes and 86 commercial units lost in the city of Santa Rosa valued at $1.18 billion. Local Politics Social Justice American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) arson california fires fires Fourth Amendment ICE detainer Jesus Fabian Gonzalez Sanctuary City Sanctuary State Santa Rosa Sonoma County U.S. Constitution Wine Country COMMENTS Please let us know if you're having issues with commenting. SOCIAL MOST POPULAR ‘Massive Support’ for Trump as Crowds Pack Nebraska Rally Trump Says Lack of Refineries, Not Strait of Hormuz, Is 'Driving Up' Gas PHOTOS: Jack Smith Wears anti-Trump 'No Kings' Shirt to Music Festival Claire Valdez Says She Pitched 'Trans Bill of Rights' to Hakeem Jeffries Raskin: 'Once We Get Back Into Power' Dems Will Subpoena Trump Family Trump: ‘Threat’ Forced U.S. Bombers from UK; Iran Will ‘Suffer Greatly Bessent: Iran Faces Zero Oil Revenue This Week — Tehran Warns of Crisis Karoline Leavitt Joining Fox News After Leaving White House Americans Turn to AI Chatbots to Decide How to Vote in Midterm Elections Rivera: 'Appalling' Trump Has Masked ICE Agents 'Preying' on Latinos FROM THE HOMEPAGE Trump: ‘Threat’ Forced U.S. Bombers from UK — Vows Iran Will ‘Suffer Greatly’ over Any Combat Drone Plot ‘Massive Support’ for Trump as Crowds Pack Nebraska Rally Karoline Leavitt Joining Fox News After Leaving White House Poll Shows Broad Consensus on Showing Valid Photo ID, Proof of Citizenship to Vote Americans Turn to AI Chatbots to Decide How to Vote in Midterm Elections Raskin: ‘Once We Get Back Into Power’ Dems Will Subpoena Trump Family DHS Buys Four Jails in California for $950 Million Trump Signs Diesel Tax Relief Order, Sec. Rollins Projects $640M in Savings for Farmers Geraldo Rivera: ‘Appalling’ Trump Has Masked ICE Agents ‘Preying’ on Latinos Report: Talarico Defended ‘Defund the Police’ Debate in 2020 Call NFL Suspends Two Refs for ‘Unprofessional Conduct’ After Player Confrontations WATCH: Arizona State Cheerleader Shoved to the Ground, Hit by Cops After Interfering Arrest BREITBART NEWS Masthead About Us Accessibility Statement Policy Info Editorial Guidelines Terms of Use Privacy Policy Advertise Contact Us Careers Store Get the App Newsletters Signup Send A Tip Sitemap Copyright © 2026 Breitbart",1,Politifact,val
